From 82684809083ac149ea8db83000411bff20e2ea38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:25:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223B: shadow quality split into independent
 settings; extShadowQuality becomes a preset

- hdShadowChar (0 off / 1 1024 / 2 2048), hdShadowCharRadius, hdShadowWorld (0 / 1024 / 2048), hdShadowWorldUpdate
  (tiles after moving / every frame), hdShadowWorldCasters (buildings / + near foliage / everything), hdShadowWorldDistance
  (cascade scale), hdShadowUnitDim. Changing extShadowQuality writes the stock combination; saved settings win on load.
- s_shadowMode is derived from them, so every mode test, the shader value and the water-reflection override behave;
  scattered tests go through CShadowCache helpers (WorldShadows, BandsEveryFrame, CharacterShadows, DimUnitsInShadow,
  PlayerMapQueryFlags, BandQueryFlags). Separate player-map and cascade sizes; cached tiles marked with 0x10.
- hdSunShadows forces world shadows on (SetWorldShadowsForced) instead of bumping and restoring the mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
